|~ What is declared under `::tag`, the kind of a tag name: its
   constructor and its refusal, the comparisons of tag names, and
   `manifest`. ~|

:tag/construct
  |~~ Reads a tag name as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/PayloadNotTagError
  |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
      tag is read by `type`.
  ~~|

:tag/construct/readsATagNameAsItself
  |~~ `::tag` over a tag name is that name. ~~|
  ::law~(::tag::Box | eq ::Box)

:tag/PayloadNotTagError/refusesAKeyword
  |~~ A keyword payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::tag:k !| [type /actualType] | eq [::tag/PayloadNotTagError ::keyword])

:tag/gt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives, `::b | gt ::a`. Tag names compare by their names as
      they are spelled, letter by letter, so a capital comes before a
      small letter, `::a | gt ::B` answering `true`, and a name comes
      before the names that go on under it, `::vec/count | gt ::vec`
      answering `true`; values sorted by `type` so fall in the order of
      the names of their kinds. A tag name compares with a tag name
      alone: a keyword, a string or any other value given is refused
      under the value, `::status | gt :open` among them. `gte` answers
      whether the subject comes after the value or is the same name,
      `lt` and `lte` the reverse.
      ::link~(::tag/gte | doc) ::link~(::tag/lt | doc)
      ::link~(::tag/lte | doc) ::link~(::keyword/gt | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gt/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value, `false` otherwise. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/gt/value
  |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against the
      subject, `::b | gt ::a`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gt/value/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gt ::a`; a keyword
      compares by the `gt` of keywords, `:b | gt :a`.
  ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gt/ordersByName
  |~~ `::b` comes after `::a`. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | gt ::a)

:tag/gt/putsACapitalFirst
  |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | gt ::B)

:tag/gt/putsANameBeforeTheNamesUnderIt
  |~~ A name comes before the names that go on under it. ~~|
  ::law~(::vec/count | gt ::vec)

:tag/gt/keepsOneNameApartFromItself
  |~~ A name does not come after itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | gt ::a | not)

:tag/gt/ordersValuesByTheNamesOfTheirKinds
  |~~ Values sorted by `type` fall in the order of the names of their kinds. ~~|
  ::law~([1 "a" :k] | sort ~(type) | eq [:k 1 "a"])

:tag/gt/value/NotTagError/refusesAKeyword
  |~~ A keyword is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | gt :a !| type | eq ::tag/gt/value/NotTagError)

:tag/gte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes after the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::b | gte ::b`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names, by their names as they are
      spelled.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/gte/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value or is the same name,
      `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/gte/value
  |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against the
      subject, `::b | gte ::a`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/gte/value/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | gte ::a`; a keyword
      compares by the `gte` of keywords, `:b | gte :a`.
  ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/gte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A name comes after or is itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | gte ::b)

:tag/gte/keepsAnEarlierNameApart
  |~~ An earlier name does not come after a later one. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | gte ::b | not)

:tag/gte/value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | gte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/gte/value/NotTagError)

:tag/lt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives, `::a | lt ::b`. It compares as `gt` does, tag names
      with tag names, by their names as they are spelled, so `::B | lt
      ::a` answers `true`.
      ::link~(::tag/gt | doc) ::link~(::tag/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lt/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value, `false` otherwise. ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lt/value
  |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against the
      subject, `::b | lt ::a`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lt/value/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lt ::a`; a keyword
      compares by the `lt` of keywords, `:b | lt :a`.
  ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lt/ordersByName
  |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lt ::b)

:tag/lt/putsACapitalFirst
  |~~ A capital comes before a small letter. ~~|
  ::law~(::B | lt ::a)

:tag/lt/keepsOneNameApartFromItself
  |~~ A name does not come before itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lt ::a | not)

:tag/lt/value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | lt 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lt/value/NotTagError)

:tag/lte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject, a tag name, comes before the tag name
      the call gives or is the same name, `::a | lte ::a`. It compares as
      `gt` does, tag names with tag names.
      ::link~(::tag/lt | doc) ::link~(::tag/gte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/lte/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value or is the same name,
      `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:tag/lte/value
  |~~ The tag name the subject is compared with, computed against the
      subject, `::b | lte ::a`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:tag/lte/value/NotTagError
  |~~ The value compared is a tag name, `::b | lte ::a`; a keyword
      compares by the `lte` of keywords, `:b | lte :a`.
  ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::tag)

:tag/lte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A name comes before or is itself. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lte ::a)

:tag/lte/ordersByName
  |~~ `::a` comes before `::b`. ~~|
  ::law~(::a | lte ::b)

:tag/lte/value/NotTagError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no tag name to compare with. ~~|
  ::law~(::b | lte 1 !| type | eq ::tag/lte/value/NotTagError)

:tag/manifest
  |~~ Answers the set of the names declared one name under the noun the
      subject names, each by its address: `::number | manifest` the
      words and the refusals of numbers, `::vec/take | manifest` the
      parts and the answer of `take`, `::qlang | manifest` the chapters
      of the language. A tag name that names nothing answers the empty
      set. The laws of a name are no part of the answer, `laws` reads
      them; the kinds of the scope `kinds` lists, and what the reader
      declared `env`; and what one name holds the axes read,
      `::vec/count | source`, `| doc`. The subject is the tag name of the
      noun: a keyword, `:number`, names a binding and no noun, and is
      refused as any other value is, and the call takes no value, so
      `manifest ::vec` is refused.
      ::snippet~(::number | manifest) ::link~(::any/laws | doc)
      ::link~(::any/kinds | doc) ::link~(::any/env | doc)
      ::link~(::any/source | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:tag/manifest/answer
  |~~ The addresses of the names declared one name under the noun. ~~|
  ::set

:tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError
  |~~ `manifest` is asked of a noun by its tag name, `::number |
      manifest`; a keyword names a binding and no noun.
  ~~|

:tag/manifest/ArgsBeyondPartsError
  |~~ `manifest` reads the noun of the subject and takes no value: the
      manifest of vectors is `::vec | manifest`.
  ~~|

:tag/manifest/holdsAVerbOfTheNoun
  |~~ The manifest of numbers holds `add`. ~~|
  ::law~(::number | manifest | has ::number/add)

:tag/manifest/holdsAChapter
  |~~ The manifest of the first page holds its chapter on values. ~~|
  ::law~(::qlang | manifest | has ::qlang/values)

:tag/manifest/holdsThePartsOfAWord
  |~~ The manifest of a word holds its parts. ~~|
  ::law~(::vec/take | manifest | has ::vec/take/count)

:tag/manifest/holdsTheNamesOfAReader
  |~~ The manifest of a reader's noun holds the names declared under it. ~~|
  ::law~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box | manifest | eq #[::Box/area])

:tag/manifest/leavesTheLawsToLaws
  |~~ The laws of a name are no part of its manifest. ~~|
  ::law~(::number/add | [(manifest | filter ~(binding | /value | is ::law) | count) (laws | count | gt 0)] | eq [0 true])

:tag/manifest/answersNothingForANameThatNamesNothing
  |~~ A tag name that names nothing answers the empty set. ~~|
  ::law~(::Nothing | manifest | eq #[])

:tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number is no noun. ~~|
  ::law~(5 | manifest !| [type /actualType] | eq [::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError ::number])

:tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError/refusesAKeyword
  |~~ A keyword names a binding and no noun. ~~|
  ::law~(:number | manifest !| type | eq ::tag/manifest/SubjectNotTagError)

:tag/manifest/ArgsBeyondPartsError/refusesANounGivenAsAValue
  |~~ A noun given as a value is refused; it is the subject. ~~|
  ::law~(::qlang | manifest ::vec !| type | eq ::tag/manifest/ArgsBeyondPartsError)
